# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The www -> apex redirect does NOT live here, and cannot. Pages' _redirects
# only accepts a RELATIVE path as the source; an absolute one is silently
# skipped, which the first build said out loud:
#
#   Found invalid redirect lines:
#     - #10: https://www.glensmokeshop.com/*  https://glensmokeshop.com/:splat  301!
#       Only relative URLs are allowed.
#
# A rule that parses, deploys, and does nothing is worse than no rule, because
# it reads as configured. Host-to-host redirects are done with a Redirect Rule
# on the zone instead (Rules -> Redirect Rules), which runs at the edge before
# Pages is reached: hostname eq "www.glensmokeshop.com" -> 301 to
# https://glensmokeshop.com with the path and query preserved.
#
# Path-level redirects, if any are ever needed, belong in this file.

# /hemp became /21-room when the Hemp Room was widened to cover kratom, kava
# and botanicals as well. A relative source IS allowed here (unlike the
# host-matching www rule that Pages rejected), so this one actually works.
/hemp  /21-room  301
